<section class="blk">
  <h2>How to add to this</h2>
  <p class="prose">The register lives at <span class="mono">data/lerena-register.tsv</span>. A person earns a
    row the moment they are seen in a record, not when they are understood. If you meet a Lerena anywhere —
    a headline, a headstone, a passenger list, a race card — the useful thing is the <em>citation</em>, not
    the conclusion. Conclusions can be drawn later; a source seen once and not written down is lost.</p>
</section>

